course: dictionary
lesson: 13394
title: Words for cattle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A heifer is a young female cow that has not yet had a calf, or has had only one. The words around it give you clues. «The farmer led the heifer into the barn.» The word farmer and the barn tell you this is about animals on a farm.
explain: «The young heifer stayed close to the gate.» Young is a clue that the heifer is not fully grown, and the gate is another clue that she lives on a farm. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A cow? A calf? Then check which one matches the clues.
explain: Farmers and scientists use a special set of cattle words. A calf is a baby. A heifer is a young female. A cow is an adult female that has had calves. A bull is an adult male. When you learn these words together, each one helps you understand the others.
fact: A heifer is a young female cow that has not yet had a calf, or has had only one.
fact: A calf is a baby cow, a heifer is a young female, and a cow is an adult female that has had calves.
fact: A bull is an adult male cow, and a bullock or steer is a young male that cannot have calves.
fact: The plural of heifer is heifers, as in «The heifers grazed in the field.»
fact: Context clues, like the words farm, field and calf, help you guess a word, and a dictionary confirms it.
exercise: «The farmer led the heifer into the barn.» What is a heifer? | *A young female cow that has not had a calf | A baby cow | A kind of horse | An adult male cow
exercise: «The calf followed its mother across the field.» Find and copy the word that means a baby cow. | *calf | field | mother | across
exercise: Which word means an adult male cow? | cow | calf | *bull | heifer
test: «The heifers grazed in the field all afternoon.» Which word tells you the cows are young and female? | *heifer | bull | cow | calf
test: Lily says a heifer and a cow are the same thing. What is the difference? | *A heifer is young and has not had a calf, while a cow is an adult female that has had calves | A heifer is an adult male, and a cow is a baby | They mean exactly the same, so there is no difference at all | A heifer is a kind of horse
exam: Which word is the best match for a young female cow that has not yet had a calf? | *heifer | steer | bull | calf
